+Ordinary renewal selects/publishes under a short monitor but performs JDBC outside it. Before completion enters any DB transaction, DRAINING_RENEWAL disables new ticks and waits boundedly without DB locks for the selected renewal to finish. Only then DISPATCHED calls queue once; after fresh DB authority/expiry checks, callback admission briefly tests loss/close. Thus completion never owns DB locks while waiting for a renewal owning its admission monitor. Close/stream abort/join remain outside blocking monitor regions; unknown completion ACK never triggers a second ordinary completion. Lease20s/heartbeat5s/poll5s and bounded drain/DB/shutdown profiles remain.
